# Copy to .env and change what you need. Both settings have defaults, so an
# empty .env - or none at all - is fine for local work.

# Port the API listens on.
PORT=3000

# One of: development, production, test.
NODE_ENV=development

# Required, no default. Matches docker-compose.yml; `closet_test` is the database
# the tests use.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://closet:closet@localhost:5432/closet

# The database the `test:db` suite writes to.
DATABASE_URL_TEST=postgresql://closet:closet@localhost:5432/closet_test

# Signs the access tokens. At least 32 characters; generate one with
# `node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"`.
JWT_SECRET=generate your own, at least 32 characters

# How often one caller may ask, per window, per address. The window is shared by
# both allowances; the second one covers sign-up, sign-in and refresh, where
# guessing pays off and the general allowance would be far too generous.
RATE_LIMIT_TTL=60
RATE_LIMIT_MAX=120
AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=10

# How many proxy hops to believe when working out who is calling. 0 means the
# socket's own address and nothing else — correct when the API is reached
# directly. Behind one reverse proxy set 1, behind a proxy and a CDN set 2.
# Too low and every caller looks like the proxy, so one of them exhausts the
# allowance for everybody. Too high and anyone can forge X-Forwarded-For and
# walk around the limit entirely.
TRUST_PROXY=0

# The origins a browser may call this API from, separated by commas. Empty
# allows nothing. Each entry is a bare origin: no path, no trailing slash —
# CORS compares the Origin header to this string exactly, so a slash makes a
# rule that never matches and the failure only shows up in a browser.
# The Vite dev server is on 5173.
#
# The bucket keeps its own copy of this list. After changing it, run
# `pnpm --filter @closet/api storage:cors` against the deployment's bucket:
# without that, browser uploads are refused with an error that names neither
# the bucket nor this setting. MinIO has no such rules and allows every origin,
# so a laptop will not warn you.
WEB_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# The refresh cookie's SameSite attribute. Keep lax while the client and the
# API are the same site — in development they differ only by port, which
# SameSite ignores. Set none when the client is served from somewhere else
# entirely (static hosting beside an API on another domain), because a lax
# cookie is not sent on a cross-site request at all: the refresh then works
# locally and silently stops working on the first day of a deployment.
# none forces Secure, so it needs https. A single domain with the client on
# app. and the API on api. is same-site and needs none of this.
COOKIE_SAMESITE=lax

# Where photographs live. The endpoint, region and addressing style default to
# the MinIO that `docker compose up` starts; the bucket and the credentials have
# no defaults on purpose, because a wrong-but-present value would have the API
# quietly reading and writing somewhere nobody meant.
#
# For Backblaze B2: the endpoint and region come from the bucket's own page
# (the region number differs per account), the key is an application key scoped
# to that one bucket rather than the master key, and path style is false —
# B2 addresses a bucket by host, MinIO by path.
S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
S3_REGION=us-east-1
S3_BUCKET=closet-photos
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=closet
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=closet-secret
S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
S3_UPLOAD_URL_TTL=300
S3_VIEW_URL_TTL=900

# Feature flags, by name, separated by commas, over their defaults in
# packages/core/src/flags/flags.constants.ts. An unknown name, or one in both
# lists, stops the API from starting. FEATURES_OFF=photoCutout keeps phones from
# downloading the background-removal model; new items keep their original photo.
FEATURES_ON=
FEATURES_OFF=

# Where a browser reaches the photo store, when that is not S3_ENDPOINT. Every
# presigned link then starts here instead. Leave unset normally; the phone mode
# (`api-phone` in .claude/launch.json) sets /storage, which Vite proxies to MinIO.
# A path or a bare origin, no trailing slash.
# S3_PUBLIC_URL=/storage
